{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141454-nightmare-dice-points","id":1141454,"title":"Nightmare Dice/Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-18T10:30:20-07:00","id":1141454,"title":"Nightmare Dice/Points","content":"Did I miss something, or is there no way to get rid of Nightmare Points? If you get a Nightmare point when you botch a Glamour roll, then you add one or more Nightmare dice, and get another point when you roll a 10. It seems to me like you'll inevitably end up with all your Willpower being imbalanced, and become bedlaminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12192-rabdos","name":"Rabdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12192_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T10:39:29-07:00","id":1141458,"title":"","content":"All of your Nightmare points clear when you hit 10 (at which point you gain an Imbalance). You can lose Imbalances through Epiphany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T10:42:19-07:00","id":1141461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141454-nightmare-dice-points?p=1141458#post1141458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can lose Imbalances through Epiphany.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, that's the part I didn't see. Thank you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12192-rabdos","name":"Rabdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12192_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}